1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,942
A peptide chain is built on a tiny bead.

2
00:00:02,942 --> 00:00:04,283
One link at a time.

3
00:00:04,283 --> 00:00:08,346
Add a link, wash, unlock the end, add the next.

4
00:00:08,346 --> 00:00:10,455
Every cycle is close to perfect.

5
00:00:10,455 --> 00:00:11,627
Never perfect.

6
00:00:11,627 --> 00:00:16,718
Even at ninety-nine percent per step, thirty links keeps about seventy-four percent.

7
00:00:16,718 --> 00:00:20,846
Skip one link, and you get a shorter chain that looks almost the same.

8
00:00:20,846 --> 00:00:23,333
That is why a vial holds more than one thing.

9
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:26,901
When the chain is done, it is cut free from the bead.

10
00:00:26,901 --> 00:00:29,036
Follow for more peptide science.

